# Optional server-read configuration. No environment file is required locally.
# Copy this file to apps/web/.env.local to configure the web application.
#
# APP_ORIGIN supplies Next.js metadataBase for relative metadata URLs. The current
# foundation has no canonical or social-image metadata that requires this value.
# Use an HTTPS origin without credentials, a path, a query or a fragment.
# HTTP is accepted only for localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1] during local development.
# APP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3000
#
# P14 optional server-only connection; leave unset for the complete frontend demo.
# DATABASE_URL must use the dedicated askbd_web role, never postgres or a service key.
# Local connection details come from the local CLI; do not commit actual values.
# P17 grants only a bounded reviewed-metadata function to askbd_web; raw tables
# remain inaccessible. Login/password provisioning is a trusted operator task.
# DATABASE_URL=
# Separate structured-feedback writer, server-only; do not reuse web/admin credentials.
# FEEDBACK_DATABASE_URL=  # dedicated askbd_feedback role; production intake stays closed
# Remote connections enforce certificate-verified TLS. No URL sslmode overrides.
# No AI key or NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable is supported.
#
# P16 optional staff identity; all settings are server-only. Leave unset for demo.
# APP_ORIGIN must match the browser origin exactly for staff form submissions.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-approved-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=  # publishable/anon key ONLY; never a service-role key
# ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=       # dedicated askbd_staff connection, never postgres
# CURSOR_SIGNING_KEY=       # 32-64 random bytes as lowercase hex, server-only
# Use `npm run auth:dev` for guarded local credentials injected in memory instead
# of writing real values here. `npm run test:integration` creates disposable users.
# Never place secrets in NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables; their values enter browser bundles.
#
# P20 server-only directory mode: demo (default) or published.
# Published uses reviewed SQL projections at request time; it never falls back to
# demonstration records on DB errors. AI/staff credentials are unnecessary for reads.
# DIRECTORY_MODE=demo
#
# Phase 7 optional server-only interface selection. demo preserves local preview;
# api uses the same-origin answers route, which remains unavailable in production.
# This does not approve/enable a provider, evidence, billing or public generation.
# CHAT_MODE=demo
# Optional server-only generation policy, disabled by default. Vertex adapter
# implementation is approved, but live calls and billing are not. Environment
# configuration alone cannot grant live authorization. See docs/VERTEX_AI.md.
# AI_PROVIDER=disabled
# AI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash         # explicit GA ID; no rolling aliases
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=            # required only for future approved ADC use
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=global      # global/us/eu; privacy review still required
# AI_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# AI_MAX_CONTEXT_BYTES=16000
# AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1024
# AI_DAILY_TOKEN_BUDGET=100000       # local reservations, not a currency budget
